today friends are remembering the  boulder city pilot who was killed in a  crash near the nevada arizona border  over the weekend 73 year old richard  mayahan died saturday when his small  plane went down to mohave county joe  moller joins us live from the boulder  city airport to share more about the  pilot joe  friends say the plane that richard was  in was a kit aircraft that he stored  here at the boulder city airport friends  tell me he was a very experienced pilot  and many are now curious about what  happened  73-year-old richard moynihan is being  remembered by many in boulder city after  a crash in northern arizona this is a  photo of a hangar at the small airport  with a message saying rest in peace  friend curtis campy says moynihan was an  experienced pilot who served in the  military he says he saw him at the  airport days before the crash and is  shocked by what happened it's a very  nice airplane i finished it about a year  and a half ago  i think there are only about 150 hours  on it  he's a pretty mellow flyer not like some  of us who like doing a little more  aerobatics and formation flying rich  really wasn't into that so  we're all really curious what happened  you know campy says moynihan's plane was  called an r-7 kit aircraft he expects he  was going for a short flight or to  somewhere for a bite to eat he says he  will be missed by many in boulder city  back out here live the faa and the ntsb  were notified about this crash and they  are investigating what exactly caused it  to go down reporting live in boulder  city joe moller live local now
 

